A longer wait for the CEF message pump while no window is on screen.

Applies to: tauri-runtime-cef 3.0.0-alpha.7 (crates.io) + 0001, 0003, 0004, 0005, 0006, 0007,
applied in vendor/tauri-runtime-cef. Not offered upstream.

Why: the pump never waits longer than cefclient's 33 ms, so its safety-net timer woke the
hidden, idle app about 31 times a second (0.76 % CPU, D59). While no window of the app is on
screen the longest wait is 1 s instead. A window counts as on screen while it is visible,
covered or not, and can be key or main (the menu-bar item's window is always visible and
holds no web content). Every window's occlusion change schedules work at once, which
replaces a long wait, so a window shown again paints and answers without waiting for it.

0005 tried a 250 ms wait while the app was inactive and no window visible, which also
counted covered windows as hidden: requests through the in-process scheme handler then
waited up to a timer's length while a window was on screen. Here a shown window, covered
or not, keeps the 33 ms cap, and only a window off screen waits longer.

